    "details": "<p><strong>Code Avengers &ndash; The Ultimate Coding &amp; Debugging Challenge:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>CODE AVENGERS is a coding and debugging competition organized as part of Tech Media Fest 2026 by Bharati Vidyapeeth's Institute of Computer Applications and Management (BVICAM), New Delhi.</li>\n<li>The competition tests participants on debugging, programming concepts, logical thinking, problem-solving, and coding skills through two technical rounds.</li>\n<li>Participants will compete individually across a debugging challenge and a final coding contest.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"eflhi8\" data-start=\"650\" data-end=\"685\">Event Date: 30th September 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1m6mptu\" data-start=\"686\" data-end=\"714\">Time: 10:00 AM onwards</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1b77bpk\" data-start=\"715\" data-end=\"752\">Venue: BVICAM Campus, New Delhi</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Format:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Debugging Challenge (Elimination Round):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"n2fp5s\" data-start=\"829\" data-end=\"884\">Participants will be given 5 buggy code snippets.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"xr1efx\" data-start=\"885\" data-end=\"943\">Identify the errors and suggest appropriate corrections.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"d3s0ml\" data-start=\"944\" data-end=\"994\">Code execution is not allowed in this round.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"6tvs0c\" data-start=\"995\" data-end=\"1023\">Time Limit: 30 minutes</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1bj30yf\" data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1079\">Top-performing participants will qualify for Round 2.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &ndash; Final Coding Contest:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"hgstcs\" data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1198\">Qualified participants will solve 3 coding problems of varying difficulty.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1ja62jk\" data-start=\"1199\" data-end=\"1263\">At least 2 problems must be solved to qualify for ranking.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1rhj64z\" data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1289\">Time Limit: 2 hours</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"13zrdfo\" data-start=\"1290\" data-end=\"1339\">Languages Allowed: C, C++, Java, and Python</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"un3eda\" data-start=\"1340\" data-end=\"1436\">Solutions will be evaluated on correctness, efficiency, readability, and coding practices.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>AI Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"19083d7\" data-start=\"1454\" data-end=\"1569\">ChatGPT, GitHub Copilot, and similar AI-assisted coding tools are strictly prohibited during the competition.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1fn9wwi\" data-start=\"1570\" data-end=\"1637\">Participants must solve and submit their solutions independently.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who Should Participate:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"xhnhuh\" data-start=\"1668\" data-end=\"1703\">Open to all college students.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"6ib0g2\" data-start=\"1704\" data-end=\"1740\">Individual participation only.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"6f1943\" data-start=\"1741\" data-end=\"1822\">Suitable for students interested in coding, debugging, and problem-solving.</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-10-03T00:00:00+05:30",
